  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday) \nIssued at 1236 PM MST Fri Nov 20 2026\n\nA weak and progressive storm system moves across the Great Basin and \nIntermountain West Monday. This will result in light to locally \nbreezy southwest winds across the western and central highlands and \nsouth winds across the eastern plains during the midday and \nafternoon hours. Ensemble cluster guidance shows this system \nbrushing northern NM late Monday afternoon into early Tuesday \nmorning resulting in some light rain and snow showers along and \nnorth of I-40. Slightly colder in the wake of the system Tuesday. \nShortwave ridging moves across the area mid Tuesday into Wednesday \nresulting in another period of tranquil weather. \n\nFor Thanksgiving Day and Black Friday, cluster guidance is still \nfairly split on two scenarios for the next storm system. The 1st and \ndrier scenario keeps the system an open wave over the central and \nsouthern Rockies before diving southeast over the central and \nsouthern Great Plains east of the state Thanksgiving evening. The \n2nd and slightly more unsettled scenario has the system diving \nsoutheast from the Great Basin to over the desert SW on Thanksgiving \nDay and potentially closing off into a low over New Mexico by \nThanksgiving night. Cluster guidance leans slightly to the 1st \nscenario (58% to 42%). Temperatures on Thanksgiving Week will be \nnear to slightly below average across western and central NM and \naround 5 to 10 degrees below average across eastern NM.",
